GitOps Overview
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the core principles and benefits of GitOps methodology
Set up and configure a local Git repository for GitOps workflows
Create Kubernetes manifests following GitOps best practices
Install and configure Argo CD on a single Linux machine
Deploy applications using Argo CD and Git-based workflows
Demonstrate how Git serves as the single source of truth for deployments
Troubleshoot common GitOps deployment issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Git version control concepts
Familiarity with Kubernetes fundamentals (pods, services, deployments)
Basic Linux command-line experience
Understanding of YAML file structure
Knowledge of container concepts and Docker basics
