Task 1: Environment Setup and Tool Installation
Subtask 1.1: Update System and Install Prerequisites
First, update your system and install essential tools:

# Update package manager
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install essential tools
sudo apt install -y curl wget git vim nano tree jq

# Install Docker
curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh
sudo sh get-docker.sh
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker

# Verify Docker installation
docker --version
Subtask 1.2: Install Kubernetes (Kind)
Install Kind (Kubernetes in Docker) for local Kubernetes cluster:

# Download and install Kind
curl -Lo ./kind https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/dl/v0.20.0/kind-linux-amd64
chmod +x ./kind
sudo mv ./kind /usr/local/bin/kind

# Verify Kind installation
kind --version

# Install kubectl
curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
chmod +x kubectl
sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/

# Verify kubectl installation
kubectl version --client
Subtask 1.3: Create Kubernetes Cluster
Create a local Kubernetes cluster using Kind:

# Create cluster configuration file
cat << EOF > kind-config.yaml
kind: Cluster
apiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4
nodes:
- role: control-plane
  kubeadmConfigPatches:
  - |
    kind: InitConfiguration
    nodeRegistration:
      kubeletExtraArgs:
        node-labels: "ingress-ready=true"
  extraPortMappings:
  - containerPort: 80
    hostPort: 8080
    protocol: TCP
  - containerPort: 443
    hostPort: 8443
    protocol: TCP
EOF

# Create the cluster
kind create cluster --config=kind-config.yaml --name=gitops-lab

# Verify cluster is running
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get nodes
Task 2: Set up Git Repository
Subtask 2.1: Initialize Local Git Repository
Create a local Git repository to serve as your GitOps source:

# Create project directory
mkdir -p ~/gitops-demo
cd ~/gitops-demo

# Initialize Git repository
git init
git config user.name "GitOps Student"
git config user.email "student@example.com"

# Create initial directory structure
mkdir -p applications/sample-app
mkdir -p argocd-config

# Create README file
cat << EOF > README.md
# GitOps Demo Repository

This repository contains Kubernetes manifests managed through GitOps principles using Argo CD.

## Structure
- applications/: Application manifests
- argocd-config/: Argo CD configuration files
EOF

# Add and commit initial files
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: GitOps repository structure"
Subtask 2.2: Create Sample Application Manifests
Create Kubernetes manifests for a sample application:

# Create namespace manifest
cat << EOF > applications/sample-app/namespace.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: sample-app
  labels:
    managed-by: argocd
EOF

# Create deployment manifest
cat << EOF > applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx-deployment
  namespace: sample-app
  labels:
    app: nginx
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.21
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "64Mi"
            cpu: "250m"
          limits:
            memory: "128Mi"
            cpu: "500m"
EOF

# Create service manifest
cat << EOF > applications/sample-app/service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nginx-service
  namespace: sample-app
  labels:
    app: nginx
spec:
  selector:
    app: nginx
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
  type: ClusterIP
EOF

# Create kustomization file
cat << EOF > applications/sample-app/kustomization.yaml
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

resources:
- namespace.yaml
- deployment.yaml
- service.yaml

commonLabels:
  managed-by: argocd
  environment: demo
EOF
Subtask 2.3: Commit Application Manifests
Add and commit the application manifests to Git:

# Add all application files
git add applications/

# Commit the changes
git commit -m "Add sample nginx application manifests"

# View commit history
git log --oneline

# Display repository structure
tree
Task 3: Install and Configure Argo CD
Subtask 3.1: Install Argo CD
Install Argo CD in your Kubernetes cluster:

# Create Argo CD namespace
kubectl create namespace argocd

# Install Argo CD
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml

# Wait for Argo CD pods to be ready
echo "Waiting for Argo CD to be ready..."
kubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=300s deployment/argocd-server -n argocd

# Verify Argo CD installation
kubectl get pods -n argocd
Subtask 3.2: Access Argo CD UI
Configure access to the Argo CD web interface:

# Get initial admin password
ARGOCD_PASSWORD=$(kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d)
echo "Argo CD Admin Password: $ARGOCD_PASSWORD"

# Port forward to access Argo CD UI
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 &
PORT_FORWARD_PID=$!

echo "Argo CD UI will be available at: https://localhost:8080"
echo "Username: admin"
echo "Password: $ARGOCD_PASSWORD"
echo "Note: Accept the self-signed certificate warning in your browser"

# Install Argo CD CLI
curl -sSL -o argocd-linux-amd64 https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64
sudo install -m 555 argocd-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/argocd
rm argocd-linux-amd64

# Login via CLI
argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --password $ARGOCD_PASSWORD --insecure
Subtask 3.3: Configure Git Repository in Argo CD
Add your local Git repository to Argo CD:

# Get the absolute path of your Git repository
REPO_PATH=$(pwd)
echo "Repository path: $REPO_PATH"

# Add repository to Argo CD (using local path)
argocd repo add $REPO_PATH --type git --name local-gitops-repo

# Verify repository was added
argocd repo list
Task 4: Create and Deploy Application using GitOps
Subtask 4.1: Create Argo CD Application Manifest
Create an Argo CD Application resource:

# Create Argo CD application manifest
cat << EOF > argocd-config/sample-app-application.yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: sample-nginx-app
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    app: sample-nginx
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: $REPO_PATH
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: applications/sample-app
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: sample-app
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
    - CreateNamespace=true
EOF

# Commit the Argo CD configuration
git add argocd-config/
git commit -m "Add Argo CD application configuration"
Subtask 4.2: Deploy Application via Argo CD
Deploy the application using Argo CD:

# Apply the Argo CD application
kubectl apply -f argocd-config/sample-app-application.yaml

# Wait for application to sync
echo "Waiting for application to sync..."
sleep 30

# Check application status
argocd app get sample-nginx-app

# List all applications
argocd app list

# Verify deployment in Kubernetes
kubectl get all -n sample-app
Subtask 4.3: Verify GitOps Workflow
Test the GitOps workflow by making changes:

# Modify the deployment to scale replicas
sed -i 's/replicas: 2/replicas: 3/' applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml

# Commit the change
git add applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml
git commit -m "Scale nginx deployment to 3 replicas"

# Trigger manual sync (or wait for automatic sync)
argocd app sync sample-nginx-app

# Verify the change was applied
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -n sample-app
kubectl get pods -n sample-app
Task 5: Demonstrate GitOps Principles
Subtask 5.1: Test Drift Detection and Self-Healing
Demonstrate how Argo CD detects and corrects configuration drift:

# Manually scale deployment outside of Git
kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5 -n sample-app

# Check current state
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -n sample-app

# Wait for Argo CD to detect drift and self-heal
echo "Waiting for Argo CD self-healing..."
sleep 60

# Verify Argo CD corrected the drift
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -n sample-app
argocd app get sample-nginx-app
Subtask 5.2: Update Application Configuration
Make additional changes to demonstrate GitOps workflow:

# Update nginx image version
sed -i 's/nginx:1.21/nginx:1.22/' applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml

# Add resource limits
cat << EOF >> applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml
        env:
        - name: ENVIRONMENT
          value: "gitops-demo"
EOF

# Commit changes
git add applications/sample-app/deployment.yaml
git commit -m "Update nginx to version 1.22 and add environment variable"

# Sync application
argocd app sync sample-nginx-app

# Verify updates
kubectl describe deployment nginx-deployment -n sample-app
kubectl get pods -n sample-app -o wide
Subtask 5.3: Monitor Application Health
Check application health and status:

# Get detailed application information
argocd app get sample-nginx-app --show-params

# Check application health
argocd app wait sample-nginx-app --health

# View application history
argocd app history sample-nginx-app

# Check sync status
kubectl get applications -n argocd
Task 6: Cleanup and Resource Management
Subtask 6.1: Application Cleanup
Clean up the deployed resources:

# Delete the application from Argo CD
argocd app delete sample-nginx-app --cascade

# Verify application is removed
kubectl get all -n sample-app
kubectl get namespace sample-app
Subtask 6.2: Stop Services
Stop running services:

# Stop port forwarding
kill $PORT_FORWARD_PID 2>/dev/null || true

