# kind delete cluster --name=gitops-lab
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Argo CD Pods Not Starting
# Check pod status and logs
kubectl get pods -n argocd
kubectl logs -n argocd deployment/argocd-server

# Restart Argo CD components if needed
kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-server -n argocd
Issue 2: Application Sync Failures
# Check application events
kubectl describe application sample-nginx-app -n argocd

# View sync operation details
argocd app get sample-nginx-app --show-operation

# Manual sync with force
argocd app sync sample-nginx-app --force
Issue 3: Repository Connection Issues
# Verify repository configuration
argocd repo list

# Test repository connectivity
argocd repo get $REPO_PATH
Key Concepts Learned
Throughout this lab, you have learned several important GitOps concepts:

Declarative Configuration: All application state is defined in Git using YAML manifests
Git as Source of Truth: The Git repository serves as the single source of truth for deployments
Automated Synchronization: Argo CD automatically syncs cluster state with Git repository state
Drift Detection: Argo CD detects when cluster state differs from Git and can automatically correct it
Self-Healing: Applications automatically return to their desired state as defined in Git
Audit Trail: All changes are tracked through Git commits, providing complete audit history
Conclusion
In this comprehensive lab, you have successfully:

Set up a complete GitOps environment on a single Linux machine using open-source tools
Created and configured a Git repository with Kubernetes manifests following GitOps best practices
Installed and configured Argo CD as your GitOps operator
Deployed applications using GitOps workflows where Git serves as the source of truth
Demonstrated key GitOps principles including drift detection, self-healing, and automated synchronization
Experienced hands-on GitOps workflows by making changes through Git and observing automatic deployments
Why GitOps Matters: GitOps revolutionizes how we deploy and manage applications by treating infrastructure and applications as code. This approach provides better security, reliability, and auditability compared to traditional deployment methods. By using Git as the source of truth, teams can leverage familiar development workflows for operations, enabling better collaboration between development and operations teams.

The skills you have learned in this lab form the foundation for implementing GitOps in production environments, where these principles scale to manage hundreds of applications across multiple clusters while maintaining consistency, security, and reliability.
